Thumbs.db

# Dart / Flutter
.dart_tool/
# 中文：**`.flutter/` 有一个例外，所以这里写成 `.flutter/*` 加一条反向规则。**
#       `.flutter/flutter_tools_gradle/` 是 Flutter 自己那个 Gradle 插件的源码副本，
#       **`android/settings.gradle.kts:16` 按路径引用它**（`file("../.flutter/flutter_tools_gradle")`），
#       所以它的 51 个文件是**故意入库**的（`c895ff8`）。
#       为什么不直接写 `.flutter/` 再加 `!`：**git 的规则是「父目录被排除时，里面的文件无法被重新包含」**，
#       所以 `.flutter/` + `!.flutter/flutter_tools_gradle/` 里的那条反向规则**是不生效的**——
#       写下去等于在记录里放一句假话。改成 `.flutter/*` 之后它才真的成立。
#       已跟踪的文件本来就不受 `.gitignore` 影响，所以这一改**不动任何现有文件**，
#       只是让**规则与仓库一致**：不写，下一个人会以为 `.flutter/` 整个不在库里。
# English: **`.flutter/` has one exception, hence `.flutter/*` plus a negation.** The
#          `.flutter/flutter_tools_gradle/` tree is a copy of Flutter's own Gradle plugin source and
#          **`android/settings.gradle.kts:16` refers to it by path**, so its 51 files are tracked on
#          purpose. A negation under an excluded *directory* would not take effect — git cannot
#          re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded — so writing `.flutter/` plus
#          `!.flutter/flutter_tools_gradle/` would put a false statement in the record. `.flutter/*`
#          makes it true. Already-tracked files ignore `.gitignore` either way, so this **moves no
#          file**; it makes the rule match the repository.
.flutter/*
!.flutter/flutter_tools_gradle/
.packages
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
build/
coverage/
dist/
docs/
# 中文：⚠️ `docs/` 是**整体**被忽略的，但里面的**手写文档是被跟踪的**（`architecture.md`、
#       `file_structure.md`、`verification.md`、`release_notes_v*.md`……）。所以**新加一篇文档必须**
#       `git add -f docs/xxx.md`，否则它会被**静默忽略**、`git status` 里连提示都没有。
#       —— 2026-10-12 就是这么发现 `release_notes_v1.1.0.md` 的：它躺在磁盘上、**从未进过仓库**，
#       而 v1.0.0 与 v1.2.0-beta.1 的发行说明都在。
# English: ⚠️ `docs/` is ignored **wholesale**, but the **hand-written documents inside it are tracked**
#          (`architecture.md`, `file_structure.md`, `verification.md`, `release_notes_v*.md`, …). A new
#          file there therefore needs **`git add -f docs/xxx.md`** or it is **silently ignored** — it will
#          not even show up as untracked. That is how `release_notes_v1.1.0.md` was found on 2026-10-12:
#          sitting on disk and **never in the repository**, while v1.0.0's and v1.2.0-beta.1's were.

